# B-bot live stubs

Real async process on the VPS. Orders are stubs. Not parquet replay.

Isolation:

- Own unit `spread-bbot.service`, log `/var/log/spread/bbot.log`, data `/data/bbot/`, backup `backup1tb:spread-bbot`.
- Never write `/data/live`, `/data/bars`, `/data/compacted`, or D backup prefixes.
- Never stop or edit `spread-collector`, D compactor, or D backup timers.
- Do not start a second N=337 book fan-out; cap CPU/RSS/FD.
- Bars: read-only `/data/bars` unless a separate decision adds bot bar sockets.

Policy is a pure function. Stub broker logs dual-leg `would_send` with place/ack/fill. No private sockets, no keys, no send. No profitability claims.

Handoff: Model Simulator owns policy; B Stub Runtime owns `app/bot/**`; Runtime Storage may add only the bot unit/paths; Validator + Validation prove D trees are untouched.

Current canary: `spread-bbot-gear2` / `/data/bbot-gear2`; GREEN closed 2026-08-30. Next is live via the B-private orchestrator, not testnet. This rule still describes the historical stub chat (`/data/bbot`, no send).
